// AutoIME manager shared phrase cases (PLAN-072 T-02/T-05).
//
// Durable author source for the phrase-management behaviour: inputs, the
// command line under test, and independent expectations. The runner
// manager/scripts/test.ps1 executes every case against the prepared launcher
// on the new ACE AV and compares exit status, stdout lines, stderr fragments
// and final file bytes.
//
// One launcher invocation per case: every launcher run compiles the Auto
// closure through the ACE front door (there is no cross-process artifact
// cache in this lane), so a case is one command over a pre-seeded data file.
// This also keeps each case inside the <=10 s per-case budget.
//
// These are CLI/file-level cases on purpose: the registered AutoDown TestCase
// recipes (auto-case) cover source-level adapters (avm/a2r/probe scalar) and
// have no recipe for an argv+files+exit contract, so this suite keeps the same
// author-source/independent-expectation discipline in the repo's JSON case
// table precedent (PLAN-071 shared/tests/cases.json). A future AutoDown recipe
// can consume this table without changing the cases.
//
// Placeholders: the runner appends `--user-data-dir <caseDir>/<user_data_dir>`
// to the step, and files are written before it runs.

